From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:53:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: pair the layers of older Matroska files; end
 a picture after its metadata

Pairing a picture's two Dolby Vision layers by timestamp is upstream's
now, in CDemuxDualLayer. This keeps the two things it does not do.

Recognize older Matroska files that carry Dolby Vision across two tracks
using their Blu-ray source IDs. Keep both tracks bound to each other even
when the file has additional video tracks, in either stream order. Honor
explicit Dolby Vision configuration records first.

Keep the enhancement picture and its brightness metadata before HEVC end
markers. Rewriting the metadata must not skip or repeat the following
part of the picture when the serialized size changes.

Both are in shared Kodi code by necessity: the tracks are told apart
where the demuxer adds its streams (DVDDemuxFFmpeg), and the end markers
are placed where the HEVC stream is rebuilt (BitstreamConverter).

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

